      "_nested_name": "title_28"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "ensure_downloaded checks for a new version at most once an hour per pack, or 15 minutes after a check that reached the server and failed. A SUCCESSFUL DOWNLOAD sets that clock too, so straight after downloading a pack, ensure_downloaded will not check again for an hour. This is by design, not a bug.",
      "_translations": {
        "value": {}
      },
      "name": "text_29",
      "_nested_name": "text_29"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "To test publishing an update: download a pack, republish it with one file changed, then press 'force update check' below. Upload the assets and the archive FIRST and the manifest LAST - a manifest landing first describes a version whose files 404.",
      "_translations": {
        "value": {}
      },
      "name": "text_30",
      "_nested_name": "text_30"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Then watch version vs available_version in the panel at the top. version only advances once every file has downloaded successfully, so a partly-applied update stays at the old version and retries on the next check. update_available means a check found a difference that has not been applied yet.",
      "_translations": {
        "value": {}
      },
      "name": "text_31",
      "_nested_name": "text_31"
    },
